cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "oligoscan: exhaustive uncapped off-target scanning for short oligos"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Du
    given-names: Jeff Guangjian
version: 0.9.4
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/breezedu/OligoScan"
url: "https://github.com/breezedu/OligoScan"
abstract: >-
  oligoscan enumerates every alignment of short oligonucleotides (siRNA, ASO;
  <=64 nt) against cDNA or whole-genome references within a user-chosen
  mismatch and indel budget. It has no mismatch cap, applies no seeding or
  filtering heuristic, and reports seed, 5'-terminal and body mismatches
  separately. Recall is exhaustive by construction and runtime is independent
  of the error budget.
keywords:
  - siRNA
  - antisense oligonucleotide
  - off-target prediction
  - sequence alignment
  - edit distance
